<title>POLAND: POLISH BOURSE CLEARS PEPEES AND GRAJEWO FOR TRADE.</title>
<headline>POLISH BOURSE CLEARS PEPEES AND GRAJEWO FOR TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The supervisory board of the Warsaw Stock Exchange approved for trade on the main market of the bourse the shares of food producer PEPEES SA and chipboard maker Zaklady Plyt Wiorowych SA w Grajewie, the bourse said.</p>
<p>It said in a Wednesday statement that Jutrzenka SA and Drosed SA were cleared to move from the parallel market to the main floor.</p>
<p>It also said that the board discussed changes in bourse regulations, but did not give any details.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
